WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.669 --> 00:00:07.100
American Horror Story has been thrilling and
terrifying audiences since 2011.

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:11.620
Although shooting one of TV's scariest series
can be a living nightmare, there aren't many

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:14.960
scenes that the American Horror Story cast
would take back.

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:18.970
But for some of the actors, things on set
got a little too real.

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:23.619
Usually, when an actor is struggling with
their lines, their main concern is that the

00:00:23.619 --> 00:00:25.890
dialogue won't be convincing enough.

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:31.880
But Gabourey Sidibe had a much more chilling
problem in one scene of American Horror Story:

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:32.880
Coven.

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:37.449
In the episode "Go to Hell," Sidibe's character
Queenie chants a Latin phrase that will summon

00:00:37.449 --> 00:00:40.489
Papa Legba, the gatekeeper to the spirit world.

00:00:40.489 --> 00:00:45.699
Given that Papa Legba is one of the American
Horror Story characters based on real people,

00:00:45.699 --> 00:00:50.109
Sidibe was understandably reluctant to disturb
the actual spirit.

00:00:50.109 --> 00:00:53.269
According to Sidibe, her concerns turned out
to be well-founded.

00:00:53.269 --> 00:00:58.190
In March 2015, during a panel titled "The
Television Academy Presents: An Evening with

00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:02.840
the Women of American Horror Story," Sidibe
said that as she was chanting, the light fixture

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:06.119
in the room started shaking, and her back
went out.

00:01:06.119 --> 00:01:10.680
When they moved on to shoot a different angle,
the light fixture crashed to the floor.

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:15.220
They resumed shooting, and that's when Sidibe
felt a finger move up her chin to her lip,

00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:16.909
which started to swell.

00:01:16.909 --> 00:01:20.730
Waiting in the makeup trailer for a medic,
Sidibe and the makeup artist could hear scratching

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:23.020
on the outside, which she described as

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:25.960
"[...] like something was trying to get in."

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:30.710
Sidibe decided the best approach was to pray,
which seemed to work, as it put an end to

00:01:30.710 --> 00:01:31.710
the noises.

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:35.969
Once home, Sidibe called her Catholic friend,
who gave her a devil-banishing prayer.

00:01:35.969 --> 00:01:40.540
Everything was peaceful until it came time
to shoot the final episode of the Coven season,

00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:44.170
which required that the rest of the cast say
the words as well.

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:47.899
When some of the ensemble found themselves
struggling with the Latin, Sidibe reluctantly

00:01:47.899 --> 00:01:49.460
agreed to say the lines again.

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:54.750
This time, she felt a finger run from her
forehead to her top lip, which immediately

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:55.750
swelled up again.

00:01:55.750 --> 00:01:57.979
"Do not do this at home, you guys."

00:01:58.979 --> 00:02:03.609
American Horror Story has treated us to many
terrifying supernatural characters.

00:02:03.609 --> 00:02:08.780
But one of the show's most disturbing monsters
was actually a human — albeit one with a

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:13.730
psychotic disposition who did not respond
well to not getting his way.

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:19.080
In American Horror Story: Freak Show, it initially
seems like the most fearsome villains will

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:24.230
be Twisty the Clown, played by John Carroll
Lynch, and Edward Mordrake, played by Wes

00:02:24.230 --> 00:02:25.230
Bentley.

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:28.930
And to be fair, you wouldn't want to run into
either of them on a dark night in the woods,

00:02:28.930 --> 00:02:30.890
or even a sunny picnic.

00:02:30.890 --> 00:02:36.230
But it was the spoiled, "freak"-obsessed Dandy,
played by Finn Wittrock, who really upped

00:02:36.230 --> 00:02:41.780
the violence and sadism — and who audiences
most wanted to see get his deserved fate.

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:46.860
Unlike Twisty and Mordrake, Dandy's murders
weren't inspired by vengeance for a lifetime

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:48.090
of abuse.

00:02:48.090 --> 00:02:52.900
He killed out of petty vindictiveness and
to feel a sense of power.

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:57.330
Freak Show was Wittrock's debut season of
American Horror Story, and one particular

00:02:57.330 --> 00:03:01.530
scene left him so shaken that he almost didn't
want to return.

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:06.829
In 2015, he told Popsugar that the scene that
bothered him the most was when Dandy massacres

00:03:06.829 --> 00:03:09.070
most of the remaining cast of the freak show.

00:03:09.070 --> 00:03:13.560
"That was actually the one day that I walked
home like, 'Argh I really hate myself and

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:14.599
don't wanna do this.'"

00:03:14.599 --> 00:03:18.650
He described his mental state afterward as
"really despondent."

00:03:18.650 --> 00:03:22.069
However, Wittrock got over that initial shock.

00:03:22.069 --> 00:03:26.700
He's since become a main fixture of the series
and the entire American Horror Story timeline.

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:32.930
Like his season-after-season co-star Sarah
Paulson, Evan Peters has been a mainstay throughout

00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:36.189
the American Horror Story anthology since
the very beginning.

00:03:36.189 --> 00:03:40.769
In fact, he's embodied some of the darkest
characters the series has ever seen.

00:03:40.769 --> 00:03:45.989
On the inaugural season, later subtitled Murder
House, Peters played teenage ghost Tate Langdon,

00:03:45.989 --> 00:03:49.970
who committed mass murder in his high school
when he was alive and continued to do terrible

00:03:49.970 --> 00:03:52.370
things as a ghost trapped in the titular home.

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:57.390
His characters on seasons 2 through 4 — Kit
Walker, Kyle Spencer, and Jimmy Darling — weren't

00:03:57.390 --> 00:04:02.579
exactly Tate-level terrifying, but his character
on season 5, the twisted serial killer James

00:04:02.579 --> 00:04:05.359
Patrick March, chilled viewers to their core.

00:04:05.359 --> 00:04:09.780
They felt the same about the handful of characters
he played on American Horror Story: Cult,

00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:12.709
which was a mix of real-life and fictional
murderers.

00:04:12.709 --> 00:04:17.510
By his own admission, Peters has felt uncomfortable
filming a number of scenes for American Horror

00:04:17.510 --> 00:04:21.560
Story, and has felt personally affected by
the subject matter at hand.

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:27.260
In a July 2018 interview with GQ, he sha red
that shooting such sinister material is, quote,

00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:31.180
"exhausting" to the point where he's questioned
his own identity afterward.

00:04:31.180 --> 00:04:32.180
Peters said,

00:04:32.180 --> 00:04:36.920
"It's really mentally draining, and you don't
want to go to those places ever in your life.

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:41.360
And so you have to go there for the scenes,
and it ends up integrating it somehow into

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:42.360
your life.

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:46.470
You're in traffic and you find yourself screaming
and you're like, 'What the hell?

00:04:46.470 --> 00:04:47.850
This isn't who I am.'"

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:52.870
He added that nude scenes on American Horror
Story have unsettled him as well — particularly

00:04:52.870 --> 00:04:55.420
one that happened in season 5.

00:04:55.420 --> 00:04:56.420
The actor shared,

00:04:56.420 --> 00:05:01.000
"A strange one was when I was Mr. March [in
American Horror Story: Hotel].

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:04.500
I was doing this butterfly razor cutting of
this poor girl.

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:07.650
[...] It was just horrific and weird and sad.

00:05:07.650 --> 00:05:11.900
[...] At that point, it was season 5, and
I was more comfortable with the crew, so it's

00:05:11.900 --> 00:05:14.020
like, 'Okay, I guess my butt will be out.'

00:05:14.020 --> 00:05:17.270
There were some earlier ones that were very
unnerving."

00:05:17.270 --> 00:05:21.850
Peters has seemingly taken all the experiences
on the chin and has done his best to separate

00:05:21.850 --> 00:05:26.190
the chaos of his professional life from the
calmness of his personal life.

00:05:26.190 --> 00:05:29.980
The actor will be back for American Horror
Story season 10, set to premiere sometime

00:05:29.980 --> 00:05:35.420
in 2021, so clearly, any scenes he's regretted
haven't kept him from the series that turned

00:05:35.420 --> 00:05:37.170
him into a household name.

